  "name": "pairwise_clamped_sigmoid_advantage_loss",
  "intuition": "This loss applies a clamp to the margin (difference between log probabilities minus advantage) to prevent extreme values that could destabilize training, then applies a sigmoid link function. Clamping ensures numerical stability and mitigates outliers, while the sigmoid models the probability that one sequence is preferred over another based on their scores and advantage, aligning with pairwise preference objectives.",
  "pseudocode": "margin = lpw - lpl - beta * advantage_gap\nclamped_margin = clamp(margin, -clip_val, clip_val)\nprob = sigmoid(alpha * clamped_margin)\nloss = -log(prob)\nweighted_loss = weight * loss\nreturn mean(weighted_loss)",
